Z||000008||olympic||08-22-2000||12:10 AM||||  I heard on one of those nature shows that the ducks/geese in the rear of the "V" make noise to encourage the ones in the front of the "V" to keep going.  The ones in the front have to do the most work because they break the head wind for the others to follow in.  Just like race cars draft(follow) each other to stay out of the wind.||||reg||1
